00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:33.529
- [Voiceover] Tyler asks,
"Do you still think the

00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:36.290
Thank You Economy will
self destruct in 2015?

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.747
Are brands living up to your
predictions slash Thank You

00:02:38.747 --> 00:02:40.837
Economy expectations?"

00:02:40.967 --> 00:02:43.867
- Tyler, once again, and I
talk about it all the time,

00:02:43.867 --> 00:02:47.067
I think things are gonna
happen sooner than they become.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:49.800
My prediction in Thank You
Economy was that people

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.760
would understand this and
then everybody would do it.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.000
And by 2015, it would get ruined.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.420
I am so off on that prediction
it's borderline embarrassing.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.141
You know, DRock, I don't know,
can you like, take my face

00:03:02.141 --> 00:03:04.000
right now and give me like, rosy cheeks?

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.780
Like, can you like make
my face red right now?

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.440
Because I'm so embarrassed
by how off I am.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.840
Because, two part.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.400
One, people just haven't
adopted the Thank You Economy.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.000
And thus, if they haven't
adopted it and scaled

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.020
and ruined it, how can it be over, right?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.100
And so, it might take a lot longer.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.640
It may take forever.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.560
More importantly, the people
that do attack the world

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.900
in a TYE world are getting dividends.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.340
I'm getting those emails.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.660
But it has not been the
landslide that I had hoped

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.260
for the consumer.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:39.620
So, my prediction was obnoxiously off.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.080
One, it may not happen,
at scale because companies

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.921
are just heartless and
just don't understand the

00:03:46.921 --> 00:03:48.180
financial benefit.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:48.978
And listen, I'm heartless.

00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:50.738
I mean it's all about the wallet with TYE.

00:03:50.738 --> 00:03:52.978
I mean to me, it's, this
is how you do business.

00:03:52.978 --> 00:03:56.118
And two, it's not enough at
enough scale or ruined yet.

00:03:56.118 --> 00:03:59.519
People are still flabbergasted
and excited when a

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:01.598
business acknowledges
them or does something

00:04:01.598 --> 00:04:03.246
half-assed caring.

00:04:03.736 --> 00:04:07.256
- Hey Gary, this is
Kyle @JockNerd and Ruby.

00:04:07.256 --> 00:04:08.416
She's two and a half.

00:04:08.416 --> 00:04:12.336
And I was wondering in the
future, how are you going to

00:04:12.336 --> 00:04:14.666
treat social media with your children?

00:04:14.896 --> 00:04:15.776
Oh no, don't hide.

00:04:15.776 --> 00:04:16.956
Say hi.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.177
Can you wave?

00:04:18.177 --> 00:04:18.995
- Oh, cute.

00:04:18.995 --> 00:04:19.716
- Hi.

00:04:19.716 --> 00:04:21.316
- Hi.

00:04:21.316 --> 00:04:22.366
- Hey.

00:04:22.366 --> 00:04:25.696
Kyle, Ruby, you know
it's been interesting.

00:04:25.696 --> 00:04:28.216
Lizzie and I, look it's hard
to find pictures of Lizzie

00:04:28.216 --> 00:04:29.256
on the internet.

00:04:29.256 --> 00:04:31.836
Let alone, you know, all full blast.

00:04:31.836 --> 00:04:33.796
And Misha and Xander are even more of a

00:04:33.796 --> 00:04:34.996
rare commodity.

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:36.710
I'm not sure.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.357
I mean, obviously, I have a
partner in crime in this answer.

00:04:40.726 --> 00:04:45.576
Lizzie, is very much the
CEO of the household.

00:04:45.586 --> 00:04:47.746
I'd like to think I'm the COO.

00:04:47.746 --> 00:04:51.372
Sometimes I'm just like, you
know, the maintenance man.

00:04:51.372 --> 00:04:53.642
No, I mean, the truth is, we
communicate a lot about this.

00:04:53.642 --> 00:04:55.442
You know, I'm a counter puncher.

00:04:55.442 --> 00:04:56.422
I talk a lot about that.

00:04:56.422 --> 00:04:57.622
I react to the time.

00:04:57.622 --> 00:05:00.300
For me to predict where
social is gonna be or

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.460
the technology.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:02.920
But what I do know is one thing.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.840
It's amazing to watch 13
year old girl behavior

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:09.160
where their spending 45
minutes on the lighting

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.120
and the angle on a Instagram photo.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.220
And then if it doesn't get
enough likes in the first

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.938
three minutes, they take it down.

00:05:14.938 --> 00:05:18.538
So clearly self esteem is very
wrapped up in these things.

00:05:18.538 --> 00:05:21.256
And every parent loves
their child so much that you

00:05:21.256 --> 00:05:23.414
want to keep them away
from bullying and being

00:05:23.414 --> 00:05:26.174
made fun of or getting into
things too early in their lives.

00:05:26.174 --> 00:05:29.374
I have the extra pressure,
in my opinion, of deciding to

00:05:29.374 --> 00:05:31.934
raise my children in
Manhattan where an 8 year old

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:34.394
maps more like a 17 year old in many other

00:05:34.394 --> 00:05:35.454
parts of the country.

00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:37.454
And so, it's a challenge.

00:05:37.454 --> 00:05:39.114
And it's something that
I think a lot about.

00:05:39.114 --> 00:05:40.534
And something I care a lot about.

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:43.034
I'm not sure exactly how
we're going to handle it.

00:05:43.034 --> 00:05:45.774
I think we're going to
handle it by instilling an

00:05:45.774 --> 00:05:48.094
enormous amount of love into our children.

00:05:48.094 --> 00:05:51.374
It's very important to us
to establish a foundation of

00:05:51.374 --> 00:05:52.674
who they are.

00:05:52.674 --> 00:05:54.275
We've been spending a lot of time of like,

00:05:54.275 --> 00:05:57.074
mission statements, and
like key pillars that we

00:05:57.074 --> 00:05:59.994
want to instill of how we
want them to act, how we

00:05:59.994 --> 00:06:03.334
want them to treat others
is very important to me.

00:06:04.472 --> 00:06:07.772
Imposing enormous self esteem into them is

00:06:07.772 --> 00:06:10.292
important to me.
And I think that to me,

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.990
there's new dynamics, but
it's still always the same

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.530
and what I mean by that is
the core pillars of good

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:19.210
parenting haven't changed
since the beginning of time.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.510
There's new dynamics.
Those things are probably

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:23.790
more important than ever.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.210
Having more self esteem,
more perseverance,

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.270
better manners, all those
things probably matter

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.370
more than ever.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:34.150
And so, I'm gonna just try
to deliver tried and true

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.090
things to my kids, much
like I do with business.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.830
The world changes, but the
principles of patience,

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.490
and believing your
people, and establishing

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:43.730
infrastructure and playing the long game.

00:06:45.528 --> 00:06:47.409
I've said it before in this show,

00:06:47.409 --> 00:06:51.974
you know, a tortoise in a
hare's costume, you know,

00:06:51.974 --> 00:06:54.664
I believe in old school things like that.

00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:58.284
So I'm just gonna instill
really good, core fundamentals

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:02.784
and let the outside world evolve
because I can't control it.

00:07:02.784 --> 00:07:05.364
And just instill my
children into that world,

00:07:05.364 --> 00:07:08.074
most prepared and best
positioned to succeed.

